body:
I've been playing around with a perfectly usual suggester case and no matter what value I use as min_doc_freq (either ridiculously high integer or any float value), I get equal results.

I'm rather new to ElasticSearch so I don't exactly understand its inner mechanisms, but if the way min_doc_freq works is much subtler than that, maybe the documentation should be improved?

I'm quoting my exact query so all parameters are explicitly set, but the same occurs for default parameters.

```

{
  "query": {
    "match_all": {}
  },
  "suggest": {
    "simple_phrase": {
      "phrase": {
        "field": "text_bigram",
        "confidence": 2.0,
        "smoothing": {
          "stupid_backoff": {
            "discount": 0.1
          }
        },
        "gram_size": 3,
        "direct_generator": [
          {
            "min_doc_freq": 1000000,
            "max_term_freq": 0.0001,
            "field": "text_raw",
            "suggest_mode": "always",
            "min_word_length": 1,
            "max_edits": 2
          }
        ],
        "real_word_error_likelihood": 0.95,
        "max_errors": 2,
        "size": 3
      },
      "text": "some text"
    }
  }
}
```

This still occurs in master - phrase suggester will return a suggestion for a term that has a document frequency lower than `min_doc_freq`, regardless of `suggest_mode`

```
PUT doc-freq
{
  "settings": {
    "index": {
      "number_of_shards": 1,
      "number_of_replicas": 0,
      "analysis": {
        "analyzer": {
